WEBVTT

00:16.510 --> 00:19.410
If my eyes are blinded by the sun

00:19.410 --> 00:24.090
I may just see the limits of the light.

00:24.090 --> 00:25.990
The mind of stardust

00:25.990 --> 00:31.830
What a small universe I live in

00:31.830 --> 00:39.370
Won't somebody give me
a code that starts at zero?

00:39.370 --> 00:41.940
Multiplied and in confusion

00:41.940 --> 00:45.970
A colony dead inside its cage

00:45.970 --> 00:50.450
Shoot your cowardly dreams

00:50.450 --> 00:53.620
Loneliness... self-destruct!

00:53.620 --> 00:58.020
No matter what sacrifices we make

00:58.020 --> 01:01.860
for a future just beyond reach

01:01.860 --> 01:05.530
Let our hearts speak to each other

01:05.530 --> 01:08.830
deep down inside

01:08.830 --> 01:12.970
Though the days just one step behind

01:12.970 --> 01:15.970
will pass even farther from us

01:15.970 --> 01:23.040
You will be in my thoughts

01:46.840 --> 01:49.670
There are two kinds of autumns.

01:49.670 --> 01:51.610
Autumns of harvest...

01:51.610 --> 01:53.700
and autumns spent lost in thought.

02:03.920 --> 02:06.850
We can finally see the town, bear-o!

02:14.960 --> 02:18.130
You know that town, Toppy?

02:18.130 --> 02:21.040
I've heard about it before, bear-o.

02:21.040 --> 02:22.900
It's the academy town of Galoa.

02:22.900 --> 02:25.540
Researchers in every
conceivable field are gathered there...

02:25.540 --> 02:29.040
and they devote themselves day
and night to their studies, bear-o.

02:29.040 --> 02:33.980
They say in Galoa you can find out
anything you'd ever want to know, bear-o.

02:33.980 --> 02:35.880
Wow...

02:38.250 --> 02:40.590
What a strange statue.

02:40.590 --> 02:45.460
"Give me your beastmen, your humans,
any and all people yearning to gain knowledge."

02:45.460 --> 02:48.130
...I've heard that's what it says, bear-o.

02:48.130 --> 02:51.300
Really? That's good for us!

02:51.300 --> 02:53.470
After what we just went
through in the Sand Sea...

02:53.470 --> 02:56.800
I'm more than ready for
a little rest and relaxation.

03:00.240 --> 03:05.200
"There are Two Kinds of Autumns"

03:17.960 --> 03:20.130
What a great place, bear-o.

03:20.130 --> 03:23.960
Yeah... I never imagined there
could ever be a place like this.

03:29.940 --> 03:32.340
Step on over!

03:32.340 --> 03:35.610
Get your hot baked sweet potatoes here!

03:35.610 --> 03:37.310
That reminds me, Morte...

03:37.310 --> 03:40.050
we haven't eaten anything all day, have we?

03:40.050 --> 03:40.980
Maybe some baked sweet potatoes...?

03:40.980 --> 03:43.180
I don't want any.

03:44.890 --> 03:47.820
What's wrong with her, bear-o?

03:47.820 --> 03:51.860
We're supposed to be the
World Destruction Committee!

03:51.860 --> 03:53.730
You don't have to start up on that again...

03:53.730 --> 03:56.130
We're already here, so let's just relax a while!

03:56.130 --> 03:57.960
I'll go buy some for us, okay?

04:02.070 --> 04:04.470
Oh, c'mon... get real!

04:04.470 --> 04:06.500
I'm telling you, it's true!

04:10.040 --> 04:13.920
I truly must thank the three
of you for all you're doing here.

04:13.920 --> 04:16.020
They've really taken a liking to you.

04:16.020 --> 04:18.490
Look how much fun they're having!

04:18.490 --> 04:21.690
A world where beastmen and
humans live together in harmony...

04:21.690 --> 04:23.730
Making that world a reality...

04:23.730 --> 04:26.250
That's my dream.

04:26.860 --> 04:28.700
Beautiful words.

04:28.700 --> 04:31.490
People can say anything...
as long as it's just words.

04:35.700 --> 04:38.670
Hey, Morte! Where are you going, bear-o?!

04:38.670 --> 04:41.110
I'm bac... huh?!

04:44.910 --> 04:49.220
She's been like that ever since we got
here on the autumn continent, bear-o.

04:49.220 --> 04:53.120
I think maybe... she's remembering some things.

04:53.120 --> 04:55.420
What sort of things is she remembering, bear-o?

04:57.090 --> 05:00.400
Let's just leave her alone for a while.

05:00.400 --> 05:02.130
So what do you wanna do now?

05:02.130 --> 05:04.130
We sure don't get many
chances like this, bear-o.

05:04.130 --> 05:08.440
I think I'll have me some sweet
potatoes and enjoy the time off, bear-o.

05:08.440 --> 05:13.110
All right. Well, as for me...
I guess I'll just walk around campus a bit.

05:13.110 --> 05:16.470
Seems like there's plenty to see around here.

06:02.760 --> 06:04.190
I'm sorry, but...

06:05.990 --> 06:08.020
we're closed right now.

06:13.170 --> 06:14.830
Is there something?

06:16.170 --> 06:17.970
I'm sorry.

06:17.970 --> 06:19.610
It's just...

06:19.610 --> 06:21.880
I've never been to this town before.

06:21.880 --> 06:25.380
I was just curious, so I...

06:25.380 --> 06:26.850
Oh, I see.

06:30.180 --> 06:32.520
Now that I think about it,
it's been quite a while...

06:32.520 --> 06:34.520
since I had some alone time.

06:34.520 --> 06:36.620
Hey, don't you think that guy's cute?

06:36.620 --> 06:41.220
Eh?! Really?! I guess he's just not my type.

06:43.300 --> 06:46.360
I sure have been on the road a long time...

06:50.870 --> 06:53.200
Sorry!

06:55.010 --> 06:57.640
Man, what a happy place!

06:59.480 --> 07:01.000
Thanks!

07:32.580 --> 07:34.420
Closing down?

07:34.420 --> 07:40.520
Yeah... I inherited this library from
my father, who used to be a historian.

07:40.520 --> 07:43.890
Between me and my big sister, the two
of us somehow managed to keep it going...

07:43.890 --> 07:48.360
but at this point I think it's just
time for me to let it go and move on.

07:48.360 --> 07:52.370
Oh... so you have an older sister.

07:52.370 --> 07:56.430
Technically, had... I suppose.

07:58.240 --> 08:02.210
Several years ago, our dad got mixed up
in a fight between beastmen and humans...

08:02.210 --> 08:04.450
and he wound up dying.

08:04.450 --> 08:07.580
After that, my sister left town...

08:07.580 --> 08:10.310
and just like that, no one
ever heard from her again.

08:11.120 --> 08:14.590
But then a few days ago, I got a notice.

08:14.590 --> 08:18.490
Just like Dad, she got herself mixed up
in a fight between beastmen and humans...

08:18.490 --> 08:20.090
and she died, too.

08:25.930 --> 08:28.570
This is... your sister?

08:28.570 --> 08:29.600
Yes.

08:29.600 --> 08:32.940
We were orphans, both of us...

08:32.940 --> 08:34.610
but Dad took us in...

08:34.610 --> 08:37.310
and raised us as brother and sister.

08:37.310 --> 08:40.920
He always said all tribes were created equal.

08:40.920 --> 08:45.490
But ever since my dad
died and my sister took off...

08:45.490 --> 08:48.020
I just couldn't stop worrying.

08:48.020 --> 08:51.190
I wondered if it was really all
right for me to keep on staying here...

08:51.190 --> 08:53.130
in a town where beastmen
and humans live side by side.

08:53.130 --> 08:58.970
But now that my sister's
been killed by beastmen too...

08:58.970 --> 09:05.370
Well anyway, that's when I decided
to close the library and get out of town.

09:11.650 --> 09:13.450
Um...

09:13.450 --> 09:16.320
I've got some time on my hands.

09:25.060 --> 09:26.790
You're late!

09:26.790 --> 09:30.000
Sorry... I forgot something
and had to go back for it.

09:30.000 --> 09:31.800
That's no excuse!

09:31.800 --> 09:33.230
Well, anyway...

09:33.230 --> 09:37.740
I guess she just doesn't like seeing
humans and beastmen getting along...

09:37.740 --> 09:39.710
poor Morte.

09:46.050 --> 09:49.550
"Historical Museum"?

09:49.550 --> 09:54.490
They say in Galoa you can find out
anything you'd ever want to know, bear-o.

09:54.490 --> 09:58.930
Maybe in there... they might know
something about the Destruct Code!

10:06.000 --> 10:10.540
So then, why did you visit this town?

10:10.540 --> 10:14.530
No reason. I just stopped here along the way.

10:16.010 --> 10:18.500
You're a woman... but traveling all alone?

10:26.250 --> 10:28.360
That's my sister's studio.

10:28.360 --> 10:33.760
She was studying
painting at the university here.

10:33.760 --> 10:37.030
I have to clean that room out too...

10:37.030 --> 10:42.140
but I haven't stepped foot in
there even once since she left.

10:42.140 --> 10:44.270
It's hard to describe...

10:44.270 --> 10:46.970
but it feels like if I go in there...

10:46.970 --> 10:49.740
all my memories of when she
was alive will just somehow fall away.

10:51.550 --> 10:53.710
I know how you feel.

11:27.350 --> 11:31.750
Well, books on those sorts of topics
don't have any real academic value...

11:31.750 --> 11:35.810
so we keep them all in one
place back here in the storehouse.

11:37.190 --> 11:41.530
We organize and organize
and still we can't keep up with it...

11:41.530 --> 11:44.100
Ah, here it is.

11:44.100 --> 11:45.970
Thanks for taking the time to help me.

11:45.970 --> 11:50.200
Oh, don't mention it. Just give
me a holler when you're done.

12:03.050 --> 12:05.490
"The Destruct Code"...

12:05.490 --> 12:08.990
"Contains the power to destroy the world"...

12:08.990 --> 12:12.560
"Since long ago, knowledge
of its existence has been held,

12:12.560 --> 12:16.830
and passed down in folk memory"...

12:16.830 --> 12:22.740
Come to think of it, I wonder where
I first heard about the Destruct Code...

12:37.220 --> 12:38.720
"Written by

12:38.720 --> 12:40.650
the Alligator Master"...

12:46.660 --> 12:51.700
Wow, this book's full of research!

12:51.700 --> 12:57.510
"The Destruct Code was formed by the
gods at the time of the world's creation.

12:57.510 --> 13:03.910
The annihilation it offers may be
carried out by either humans or beastmen."

13:03.910 --> 13:09.680
It's pretty detailed... I wonder if it
has something about how to use it.

13:09.680 --> 13:11.220
Excuse me!

13:11.220 --> 13:13.190
Be right there!

13:16.120 --> 13:19.230
Could I maybe borrow this book for a while?

13:19.230 --> 13:22.630
Oh sure, sure... if you
want, I'll even give it to you.

13:22.630 --> 13:26.120
We could keep it here, but it's not
like anyone's ever gonna read it anyway.

13:37.710 --> 13:39.080
Huh?

13:43.880 --> 13:45.950
You there!

13:45.950 --> 13:47.050
Yes?

13:58.400 --> 14:03.640
So at that point, Morte voluntarily
offered to help you, a beastman?

14:03.640 --> 14:05.070
That's right.

14:08.280 --> 14:11.780
Was there something wrong with that?

14:11.780 --> 14:13.580
Ah, no...

14:19.690 --> 14:24.850
But I suppose it's about
time I put an end to it, isn't it?

14:30.160 --> 14:32.000
Um...

14:32.000 --> 14:35.170
Thank you so much for helping me out.

14:35.170 --> 14:37.470
But don't you think it's
about time we called it a day?

14:37.470 --> 14:39.540
It's already getting dark.

14:39.540 --> 14:41.530
I guess you're right.

14:48.780 --> 14:52.220
But no, let's keep on going
until we're all the way done.

14:52.220 --> 14:55.460
If you're leaving, the sooner the better.

14:55.460 --> 15:00.720
Oh... all right. I'll go get us some light.

16:12.970 --> 16:14.470
Morte...

16:14.470 --> 16:16.640
What?

16:16.640 --> 16:19.210
The Destruct Code...

16:19.210 --> 16:22.280
Where'd you get it, anyway?

16:22.280 --> 16:27.380
My brother had it on him when he died.

16:27.380 --> 16:30.480
There was something
written about it in this book.

16:30.480 --> 16:32.390
It says there are lots of theories...

16:32.390 --> 16:37.730
but that there's no record of anyone
ever having seen the actual Destruct Code.

16:37.730 --> 16:40.160
I tried looking in some other sources...

16:40.160 --> 16:46.160
but none of them had anything saying
that what you have is the Destruct Code.

16:46.730 --> 16:51.170
What are you saying?
That my brother left behind a fake?

16:51.170 --> 16:53.410
That's not what I'm saying.

16:53.410 --> 17:00.110
But even if it is the real thing,
if we don't know how to use it, then...

17:00.110 --> 17:04.290
It doesn't matter...
I still have to put an end to this...

17:04.290 --> 17:06.580
this awful world.

17:15.830 --> 17:18.760
Where'd those two run off to, bear-o?

17:22.000 --> 17:25.470
A town like this where humans and
beastmen live together in the same place...

17:25.470 --> 17:28.640
It seems like the idea
doesn't really sit well with you.

17:28.640 --> 17:30.540
But what about the three of us?

17:30.540 --> 17:32.810
We do all right together, don't we?

17:32.810 --> 17:37.280
I'm not on this journey
to make friends, you know.

17:37.280 --> 17:41.520
So... you haven't felt that any
part of this journey's been fun?

17:47.700 --> 17:50.560
Well, I'm having a lot of fun.

17:50.560 --> 17:53.970
I mean, I've never done
anything like this before.

17:53.970 --> 17:57.370
Of course we've almost
died quite a few times...

17:59.170 --> 18:03.010
but before this I always lived by myself.

18:03.710 --> 18:06.750
Hey, remember the café where we met?

18:06.750 --> 18:11.820
Before I started working there,
I just hopped around from town to town.

18:11.820 --> 18:15.320
My life was always in danger,
just because I was a human.

18:15.320 --> 18:18.990
It didn't take long before I started
pretending to be a beastman instead.

18:18.990 --> 18:20.430
But even then...

18:20.430 --> 18:25.830
I still don't feel like I ever got a
really good night's sleep, you know?

18:26.570 --> 18:28.070
And this stupid thing!

18:28.070 --> 18:30.700
I never let it leave my side.

18:30.700 --> 18:34.610
A thing like this was all I had to rely on.

18:36.180 --> 18:42.080
Morte, is the reason you're helping him out...
because he looks like your brother?

18:45.590 --> 18:48.360
I've been meaning to ask you
this for a long time now, but...

18:48.360 --> 18:51.860
the whole reason you're so
fixated on world destruction...

18:51.860 --> 18:55.730
Isn't it just because of
what happened to your brother?

18:55.730 --> 18:59.900
Your brother was a member
of the Golden Lions, right?

18:59.900 --> 19:03.100
That's how he got caught
up in the struggle and...

19:03.100 --> 19:04.430
Stop it!

19:25.430 --> 19:28.830
I guess it's still hard for you to go in?

19:28.830 --> 19:32.000
Yes, I guess it is.

19:32.000 --> 19:35.000
I think the reason why my sister left...

19:35.000 --> 19:38.170
why she left this town where
beastmen and humans live side by side...

19:38.170 --> 19:41.510
is because she must've blamed
the town for what happened.

19:41.510 --> 19:43.740
You really think that's it?

19:43.740 --> 19:48.150
Maybe she felt like your father did,
that all tribes are created equal...

19:48.150 --> 19:54.180
and she left to go spread the
message to other people outside the town.

19:56.990 --> 19:59.080
I'm opening the door now.

20:30.290 --> 20:32.330
Yeah...

20:32.330 --> 20:34.900
You know it's just not that easy...

20:34.900 --> 20:36.660
to forgive.

20:47.910 --> 20:49.910
Let's clean it up, shall we?

20:49.910 --> 20:52.170
Do you mind staying and helping out?

21:10.760 --> 21:12.860
Eor...

21:52.940 --> 21:55.370
My sister...

22:21.100 --> 22:24.610
The glimmering seas of sand

22:24.610 --> 22:27.740
The end of the green earth

22:27.740 --> 22:33.810
Memories overflowing from the sky

22:33.810 --> 22:36.980
now plunged into darkness

22:36.980 --> 22:40.190
The memories will pile up

22:40.190 --> 22:46.190
like mounds of rubble

22:46.190 --> 22:49.430
Mutual encounters

22:49.430 --> 22:52.500
Misunderstood feelings

22:52.500 --> 22:55.640
Interwoven words

22:55.640 --> 22:58.770
People hurting each other

22:58.770 --> 23:10.880
Does the path we walk on
still lead us to tomorrow?

23:13.690 --> 23:17.520
Living this moment against the world

23:17.520 --> 23:20.560
isn't just about changing the world

23:20.560 --> 23:26.130
We're off on a distant journey across the waves

23:26.130 --> 23:29.700
So let our living heartbeat echo in the wind

23:29.700 --> 23:33.240
Around the world, to the end of the world

23:33.240 --> 23:39.210
Until we reach

23:39.210 --> 23:50.820
the promised land just beyond

23:52.930 --> 23:55.360
Wel-come- to- Clock- Town-

23:55.360 --> 23:57.200
Why're you talking like that, bear-o?!

23:57.200 --> 23:58.770
When in Clock Town,
do things the Clock Town way!

23:58.770 --> 24:00.600
C'mon, you two try
practicing your robot voices too!

24:00.600 --> 24:02.540
I don't think so.

24:02.540 --> 24:05.240
Next- time- on- World- Des-truc-tion...

24:05.240 --> 24:06.770
Ep-i-sode- 10...

24:06.770 --> 24:09.740
"There Are 108 Laws of Clockwork Robotics."

24:09.740 --> 24:12.010
Mor-te-, you- and- me- are- friends-, cor-rect-?

24:12.010 --> 24:15.250
Why- don't- you- loos-en- up- a- bit-?

24:15.250 --> 24:19.220
You- are- al-so- our- friend...

24:19.220 --> 24:20.210
bear-o.
